<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ilsharah Yahdub</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ilsharah Yahdub was a king of Saba and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhu-raydan">Dhu Raydan</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marib">Marib</a> with his brother Ya'zil Bayyin around the late second or early third century CE. Their inscriptions, dedicated at the Awwam temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almaqah">Almaqah</a>, record wars against Himyar, Hadramawt and Aksumite forces in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. He was one of the last strong rulers of an independent Saba.</p></div>
